    term: 'Second Term',
    contentHTML:
      '\n<div class="learn-intro">\n  Public companies can be further classified as <span class="learn-keyword">quoted</span> or <span class="learn-keyword">unquoted</span>, depending on whether their shares are officially listed for trading on a recognized stock exchange.\n</div>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">1. Definitions</h3>\n<p class="learn-p">A quoted (or listed) company is one whose shares are officially listed and traded on a recognized stock exchange, such as the Nigerian Exchange (NGX). An unquoted (unlisted) company is one whose shares are NOT listed on any stock exchange, even if it is a public company — its shares may still be bought and sold privately, just not through the formal exchange.</p>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">2. Key Differences</h3>\n<div class="learn-table-wrap">\n  <table class="learn-table">\n    <thead><tr><th>Feature</th><th>Quoted Company</th><th>Unquoted Company</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Stock exchange listing</td><td>Listed on a recognized stock exchange</td><td>Not listed on any stock exchange</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Share price</td><td>Publicly known and updated regularly</td><td>Not publicly quoted; harder to determine market value</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Liquidity</td><td>Shares easily bought/sold on the exchange</td><td>Shares harder to buy/sell (less liquid)</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Disclosure requirements</td><td>Stricter, ongoing disclosure to the exchange and regulators</td><td>Fewer ongoing public disclosure obligations</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">3. Examples of Quoted Companies in Nigeria</h3>\n<p class="learn-p">Well-known examples of companies listed on the Nigerian Exchange (NGX) include Dangote Cement Plc, MTN Nigeria Communications Plc, Guaranty Trust Holding Company Plc (GTCO), Nestlé Nigeria Plc, and Zenith Bank Plc, among others.</p>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">4. Requirements for Listing on the Stock Exchange</h3>\n<p class="learn-p">To be listed, a company must typically meet requirements such as: a minimum share capital threshold, a minimum number of years in profitable operation, publication of audited financial statements, a minimum free float (percentage of shares available to the public), and approval from the relevant securities regulator (in Nigeria, the Securities and Exchange Commission — SEC).</p>\n\n<div class="learn-tip-box">\n  <span class="learn-tip-icon">💡</span>\n  <strong>Exam Tip:</strong> Don\'t confuse "public company" with "quoted company" — all quoted companies are public companies, but not all public companies are quoted! A public company can remain unquoted if it chooses not to list on a stock exchange.\n</div>\n\n<div class="learn-tip-box">\n  <span class="learn-tip-icon">🎯</span>\n  <strong>Summary:</strong> Quoted companies have their shares officially listed on a stock exchange, offering greater liquidity and public price transparency but facing stricter disclosure requirements, while unquoted companies (even if public) are not listed and trade shares less formally.\n</div>\n  ',
