    contentHTML:
      '\n<div class="learn-intro">\n  The <span class="learn-keyword">financial system</span> is the network of institutions, markets, and instruments that channel funds from savers to borrowers, playing a vital role in a nation\'s economic growth and development.\n</div>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">1. Meaning of the Financial System</h3>\n<p class="learn-p">The financial system consists of all institutions, markets, and regulatory frameworks that facilitate the flow of funds between those who have surplus funds (savers/investors) and those who need funds (borrowers/businesses), enabling economic activities like investment, trade, and consumption.</p>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">2. Components of the Financial System</h3>\n<div class="learn-table-wrap">\n  <table class="learn-table">\n    <thead><tr><th>Component</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Money market</td><td>Deals in short-term financial instruments (less than 1 year), e.g., treasury bills, commercial papers</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Capital market</td><td>Deals in long-term financial instruments (more than 1 year), e.g., shares, bonds, debentures</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Banking system</td><td>Commercial banks and other deposit-taking institutions that accept deposits and provide loans</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Insurance sector</td><td>Provides risk protection/compensation in exchange for premiums</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Pension funds</td><td>Collect and invest contributions to provide retirement income for workers</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">3. Importance of the Financial System to Economic Growth</h3>\n<p class="learn-p">A well-functioning financial system mobilizes savings and channels them into productive investment, facilitates efficient allocation of capital to businesses with the best opportunities, provides a mechanism for managing risk (through insurance and diversified investment), supports government fundraising through bonds, and enables individuals to plan for retirement through pension funds.</p>\n\n<div class="learn-tip-box">\n  <span class="learn-tip-icon">💡</span>\n  <strong>Exam Tip:</strong> Remember the key distinction: Money Market = SHORT-term instruments (under 1 year); Capital Market = LONG-term instruments (over 1 year). This is one of the most commonly tested distinctions in this topic.\n</div>\n\n<div class="learn-tip-box">\n  <span class="learn-tip-icon">🎯</span>\n  <strong>Summary:</strong> The financial system connects savers with borrowers through components like the money market, capital market, banking system, insurance sector, and pension funds, playing a critical role in mobilizing savings, allocating capital efficiently, and supporting overall economic growth.\n</div>\n  ',
