    contentHTML:
      '\n<div class="learn-intro">\n  Before a company can raise funds through the <span class="learn-keyword">capital market</span>, it must satisfy a range of legal, financial, and regulatory requirements designed to protect investors and maintain market integrity.\n</div>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">1. Legal/Regulatory Requirements</h3>\n<p class="learn-p">A company must typically be properly incorporated as a public limited company, obtain approval from the relevant securities regulator (in Nigeria, the Securities and Exchange Commission — SEC), and comply with the rules of the specific stock exchange (e.g., the Nigerian Exchange) if seeking a listing.</p>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">2. Financial Requirements</h3>\n<div class="learn-table-wrap">\n  <table class="learn-table">\n    <thead><tr><th>Requirement</th><th>Purpose</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Minimum share capital</td><td>Ensures the company has sufficient scale to justify public investment</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Track record of profitability</td><td>Demonstrates the company has a proven, viable business model</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Audited financial statements</td><td>Provides verified, reliable financial information to potential investors</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Minimum free float</td><td>Ensures a sufficient percentage of shares are available for public trading, supporting liquidity</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">3. Disclosure Requirements</h3>\n<p class="learn-p">Companies must prepare a detailed Prospectus (for public issues) disclosing key information: business operations, financial performance, risk factors, management structure, and intended use of the funds raised. This transparency protects investors from making uninformed decisions.</p>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">4. Corporate Governance Requirements</h3>\n<p class="learn-p">Companies seeking to access the capital market are often required to demonstrate good corporate governance practices, such as having an independent board of directors, proper internal controls, and adherence to relevant codes of corporate governance.</p>\n\n<div class="learn-tip-box">\n  <span class="learn-tip-icon">💡</span>\n  <strong>Exam Tip:</strong> Remember that requirements exist to protect INVESTORS by ensuring companies are financially sound, transparent, and well-governed before being allowed to raise public funds — this rationale is often tested directly.\n</div>\n\n<div class="learn-tip-box">\n  <span class="learn-tip-icon">🎯</span>\n  <strong>Summary:</strong> Accessing the capital market requires companies to meet legal/regulatory requirements (proper incorporation, SEC approval), financial requirements (minimum capital, profitability track record, audited statements), disclosure requirements (Prospectus), and good corporate governance standards.\n</div>\n  ',
