    contentHTML:
      '\n<div class="learn-intro">\n  A well-functioning <span class="learn-keyword">capital market</span> delivers significant benefits to companies, investors, and the wider economy, playing a central role in national economic development.\n</div>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">1. Benefits to Companies</h3>\n<p class="learn-p">The capital market gives companies access to long-term capital for expansion and investment, an alternative to costly bank borrowing, enhanced public profile and credibility, and a mechanism to determine the market value of the business (useful for mergers, acquisitions, and succession planning).</p>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">2. Benefits to Investors</h3>\n<div class="learn-table-wrap">\n  <table class="learn-table">\n    <thead><tr><th>Benefit</th><th>Explanation</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Investment opportunities</td><td>A wide range of shares and bonds to choose from, suited to different risk appetites</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Liquidity</td><td>Quoted shares can be readily bought and sold on the exchange</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Potential returns</td><td>Opportunity to earn dividends and capital gains as share prices rise</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Diversification</td><td>Ability to spread investment risk across multiple companies/sectors</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">3. Benefits to the Economy</h3>\n<p class="learn-p">The capital market mobilizes domestic savings into productive investment, supports job creation as businesses expand, attracts foreign investment (boosting foreign exchange inflows), enables efficient allocation of capital toward the most promising businesses, and provides the government with a means to finance public projects through bonds.</p>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">4. Benefits to Government</h3>\n<p class="learn-p">Beyond raising funds through bonds, government also benefits indirectly: a thriving capital market boosts overall economic activity and corporate profits, increasing tax revenue, and provides a visible indicator of investor confidence in the national economy.</p>\n\n<div class="learn-tip-box">\n  <span class="learn-tip-icon">💡</span>\n  <strong>Exam Tip:</strong> When answering "benefits of the capital market" questions, structure your answer by stakeholder group (companies, investors, economy, government) — this earns more marks than a random unstructured list.\n</div>\n\n<div class="learn-tip-box">\n  <span class="learn-tip-icon">🎯</span>\n  <strong>Summary:</strong> The capital market benefits companies (access to capital, credibility), investors (opportunities, liquidity, returns, diversification), the economy (savings mobilization, job creation, foreign investment), and government (financing, tax revenue), making it central to overall economic development.\n</div>\n  ',
